# pico2_usb_host

A pico2-arm with a second USB port on GP2 (D+) and GP3 (D-), which Pico-PIO-USB
drives as a USB host through the RP chip's PIO, for a USB flash drive: mm.mcu's
storage calls read and write it. The native USB port stays the USB console.
The system clock is 120 MHz, a multiple of 12 MHz as Pico-PIO-USB needs.

Wiring: a USB-A socket's D+ to GP2 and D- to GP3, each through a 22-ohm
resistor, VBUS to 5 V (VBUS on a USB-powered Pico), and ground to ground.
